# shared_probe SPIR-V evidence - what each probe module DECLARES as workgroup memory.
# 'Variable Workgroup' is SPIR-V's storage class for GLSL `shared`. Both sd and sp point at the
# same array type (id 36 here), whose element count is the printed Constant, so the module asks
# for 2 x n x 4 B of workgroup memory - the byte figure in each banner is derived from those two
# numbers, the Constant/TypeArray/Workgroup lines are the primary evidence.
# Generated with: glslang -V -H shaders/probe_shm_nNNNN.comp

